  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG-AUS Transport Sector Support Program Ph 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s support to Papua New Guinea&#x2019;s transport sector is delivered through the Papua New Guinea-Australia Transport Sector Support Program (TSSP). TSSP commenced in 2007 as a 15-20 year commitment to support the Government of Papua New Guinea to achieve a well-maintained transport infrastructure network. 

Funds under this investment provides capacity building and technical assistance for governance, providing support services for the transport sector coordination body (TSCMIC) and Secretariat, policy advice, strategic direction, financial and procurement oversight for the program, monitoring and evaluation. 

TSSP2 is currently scheduled to run until 2022.


Sector split: Transport and Storage 100%</narrative>
  </description>
